# issue: 782
# red_on: 3cdf10ef; step 1 (query) fails with `resource limit exceeded for query_memory_bytes: actual 157286414, limit 157286400`, while engine v1 returns the row.
# notes: 1024 sources know one hub and the hub knows 1024 targets: 1,050,624
# notes: one-or-two-hop pairs, more than the default 150 MiB query budget admits when
# notes: the expand keeps every pair (about 214 bytes each on the red commit, 225 MB
# notes: for the set). Step 1 pins that an unordered trailing limit answers under
# notes: that budget: the pairs leave a chunk at a time, and every destination is
# notes: `reached`, so any one row is right. Step 2 counts the pairs, so a chunk
# notes: dropped or duplicated is a wrong count. Seed names: s0000..s1023 know
# notes: `hub`, `hub` knows t0000..t1023; resize by regenerating both ranges.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
node Person {
    name: String @key
    role: String
}

edge Knows: Person -> Person

